WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.830
- [Inae] I like making food item as a cake

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.794
because it's a really
easy to make to be real.

00:00:05.794 --> 00:00:08.273
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.273 --> 00:00:09.340
Hi, I'm Inae.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.930
I'm an illusion cake artist.

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:14.210
Today, we're going to make
fast food burger cake.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.590
This is cherry cake batter.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.040
Adding some oil.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.040
Adding some milk.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.190
Whisk until you don't see any cake crumbs.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.800
And I'm going to add cherries.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.070
The eggs.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.340
Mix it really good.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.280
Mix until you don't see any eggs.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.460
Going to add a little bit
of red food coloring to it.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.000
I picked red and yellow

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.610
because McDonald's has red and yellow.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:38.670
This reminds me of Halloween.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.400
It's my favorite holiday.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.540
I have lemon cake batter already mixed.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.373
Going to add.

00:00:43.373 --> 00:00:44.760
A little bit of oil.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.230
You can use whisk or a spatula.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.760
Just want to make it really nice.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.410
I'm going to add lemon juice.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:56.013
Then you can also add a little
bit a yellow food coloring.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:01.140
Okay, so I'm going to
pour lemon cake batter.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.461
This cake batter looks
like ketchup and mustard

00:01:04.461 --> 00:01:06.200
(laughing)
And I love it.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.150
Spread into a pan.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:10.899
Cherry cake goes into pans.

00:01:10.899 --> 00:01:12.630
(upbeat music)

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.920
Spread it really nice.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.616
And I usually go tap tap tap.
(pan tapping)

00:01:18.616 --> 00:01:21.199
(upbeat music)

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:25.670
I'm going to carve this cake.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:27.430
It looks like burger buns.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:30.130
First, I'm going to use cutter.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:31.420
Then I'm going to carve it.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.220
All right, this is done.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.270
And this is going to be my bottom.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.570
The bottom one is not as round as top one

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.150
because the bottom one is more flat.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.360
Cut just a little bit on top
and then flip upside down.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.310
And this is going to be my bottom bun.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.160
Time to make cake pops.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:52.160
We just need one scoop of buttercream,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.880
and then mix really good
with the cake crumbs.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.830
So this lemon cake is
going to be two patties

00:01:58.830 --> 00:01:59.913
for the cake burger.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.460
And I'm going to put this in the fridge

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.650
so that it gets a little sturdy.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:08.700
Frosting time.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.130
So I made this beautiful
cream cheese frosting,

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:17.010
and I like to use this plastic
scraps to make it smooth.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.990
Okay, I'm going to put it in the fridge.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.100
Okay, here is my lemon cake pop.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.823
I'm going to frost with chocolate ganache.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.143
And this is for the burger patty.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.210
Okay, it looks like a patty already.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.710
We have top bun.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.810
And I'm going to use modeling chocolate

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.510
to cover this bun.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:38.020
Corn starch to sprinkle on the table

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:41.430
so that modeling chocolate
doesn't stick on the table.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.593
And I use a rolling pin to make
chocolate a little thinner.

00:02:46.744 --> 00:02:50.150
(upbeat music)

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:54.604
And use a cutter to cut the
excess of modeling chocolate.

00:02:54.604 --> 00:02:55.437
Going to cut it.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.220
Tuck in little more.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.380
Then I like to press some lines

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.030
so that it doesn't look
like perfectly round

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.530
because all buns doesn't look same.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.280
Okay, here's my patty.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.110
I would like to cover with
the modeling chocolate

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.530
with little bit of brown food coloring

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.930
so that it matches patty color.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.570
Sprinkle cornstarch.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:22.115
Make sure it doesn't stick on the table.

00:03:22.115 --> 00:03:24.698
(upbeat music)

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.850
And I would like to use this piece of foil

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.530
to create the texture of a patty.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.860
Sometimes I like to use everything
I can find in my kitchen

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.890
or just my house.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:46.720
And this foil will make
perfect texture of a patty.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.750
I'm going to airbrush the top bun.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.360
And this is food coloring.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.612
I mixed with a brown,
orange, and yellow color.

00:03:53.612 --> 00:03:56.195
(upbeat music)

00:03:58.873 --> 00:04:01.123
(spraying)

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:08.160
I'm going to paint patty
with edible food paint.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.588
I use regular paintbrush
from regular art store.

00:04:12.588 --> 00:04:15.110
(upbeat music)

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.430
I went to culinary school in the city.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.860
I was watching TV and "Cake Boss" was on.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.380
It seemed like, oh, I think I can do that.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:25.090
But I have no idea what they're using.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.850
So I started to search.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.690
They have this one-day program

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.880
that you make a birthday cake.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.470
I went there, I made a birthday cake,

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.480
and it turned out really good.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.133
It was first time I ever baked cake.

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:38.966
(laughing)

00:04:38.966 --> 00:04:41.150
I'm going to paint a little bit of glaze

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:44.230
to look more juicy looking patty.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:46.190
I'm going to sprinkle some sugar.

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:47.440
Patty's done.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.400
This is a gelatin, and
it's going to be onion.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.220
And I'm chopping onions.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.320
No, actually gelatin.
(laughing)

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.260
I made a white chocolate ganache

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:01.340
and add that a bit of
red and orange coloring.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.300
Looks like Big Mac sauce.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.590
And I'll mix together
with my gelatin onion.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.380
I'm using wafer paper to make lettuce.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:13.580
So first, I'm going to petal
dust with a green color.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.050
Randomly spread it.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.605
Cut little pieces.

00:05:17.605 --> 00:05:19.310
(tearing)

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.120
Spray water.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.260
Put it on the mold.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.720
This mold is for flower petal.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.770
Just give a little bit of texture.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:30.310
And you can kind of just rip it.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.440
And looks like lettuce.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.940
We're going to make American cheese.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.820
I'm using modeling chocolate.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:39.390
Sprinkle lit bit of
cornstarch before I mix it.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:42.445
Yellow modeling chocolate,
a little bit of red.

00:05:42.445 --> 00:05:44.770
(upbeat music)

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.330
Ta-dah, yay.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:48.170
Okay, let's make a pickle.

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.070
I'm using modeling chocolate.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:55.070
So I like to use this serrated
knife for the edge of pickle.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:56.810
Just cutting it.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:01.750
And then I use this tool to
make a little bit more pickley.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.490
See?
Easy.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.790
Then, I would like to give
a little bit of texture

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:06.900
on pickle too.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.470
Let's paint it.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.930
I feel like there is no between.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.624
Either you like pickle
or you don't like pickle.

00:06:12.624 --> 00:06:13.457
(laughing)

00:06:13.457 --> 00:06:15.040
Okay, it's done.
Pickle.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.600
Time to build a burger.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:21.360
I'm putting cream cheese
frosting between bun and patty.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.850
Cheese time.

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:25.690
(dramatic music)

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.280
This is Big Mac sauce.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.830
That's really chunky.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:31.610
Add some lettuce.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:35.120
I like to have a model
when I paint something real

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.035
so I can get exact color and texture.

00:06:39.035 --> 00:06:40.060
(upbeat music)

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.133
We want to put middle bun.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.510
We just need a tiny bit
of cheese at the end

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.943
because we just going to see the edge.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.250
Some pickles.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:53.110
I personally love pickles.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.860
So I'm going to put extra pickles.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:56.813
More lettuce.

00:06:57.773 --> 00:07:00.523
(dramatic music)

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:10.693
I'm using modeling chocolate
to make tiny Sesame seeds.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:17.090
And I'm using torch to make
sauce look more runny looking.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:22.000
Then I'm going to use a
little bit of glaze on pickle

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.070
because pickle always has water.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.093
Okay, it's done.

00:07:26.093 --> 00:07:28.676
(upbeat music)

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.690
That's assembled Big Mac cake.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.842
Let's cut it and see what happens.

00:07:40.842 --> 00:07:44.180
(upbeat music)

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:48.013
That's the completed
fast food hamburger cake.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:50.080
Thank you for watching.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.322
Let us know what you guys think.

00:07:52.322 --> 00:07:53.155
(upbeat music)

00:07:53.155 --> 00:07:54.200
- [Man] Oh yes!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.867
(upbeat music)

